  "tagline": "The Linux Foundation's BSD-licensed fork of Redis, now the default engine on AWS and Google Cloud.",
  "description": "Valkey was forked from Redis 7.2.4 in March 2024, days after Redis left the BSD license, by maintainers from AWS, Google, Oracle, Ericsson and others under the Linux Foundation. It stays wire- and data-compatible with Redis OSS while shipping its own work: multi-threaded I/O, per-field hash TTLs, multiple databases in cluster mode (9.0) and database-level ACLs (9.1). For anyone who wants a drop-in Redis that stays permissively licensed and vendor-neutral, it is now the safe default, and ElastiCache, MemoryDB and Memorystore all lead with it.",
